  "description": "Florida's 11th Congressional District is an open seat in 2026 following the retirement of eight-term Republican incumbent Daniel Webster, who announced on April 28, 2026, that he would not seek re-election. The district covers all of Sumter County, most of Lake County, and part of western Orange County in Central Florida, and has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+7. The Republican primary is highly contested with multiple candidates including former state Senator Carey Baker and Lake County Commissioner Anthony Sabatini, while the Democratic primary features three contenders. The general election is rated as 'Solid Republican' by Cook Political Report, as the district gave Donald Trump 57% of the vote in 2024.",
